[0.331, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[G\r\n\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[39m Perfect! I've analyzed the codebase and task requirements. Here's my proposed solution:\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mProposed Solution\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mAnalysis\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  The application currently has:\r\n  - \u001b[1mHeader component\u001b[22m with a Plus button that triggers task creation (frontend/src/components/Header.tsx:34-41)\r\n  - \u001b[1mKanbanBoard component\u001b[22m that manages the \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcreateDialogOpen\u001b[39m state and passes \u001b[38;2;177;185;249monCreateTask\u001b[39m callback to Header (frontend/src/components/kanban/KanbanBoard.tsx:229)\r\n  - \u001b[1mTaskDialog component\u001b[22m that opens when \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcreateDialogOpen\u001b[39m is true\r\n\r\n  Currently, there are no keyboard event handlers in the codebase, so we'll need to add one.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mImplementation Plan\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m1. Add keyboard shortcut handler to KanbanBoard\u001b[22m (frontend/src/components/kanban/KanbanBoard.tsx)\r\n  - Add a \u001b[38;2;177;185;249museEffect\u001b[39m hook that"]
[0.000, "o", " listens for the 'n' key press\r\n  - Ensure it only triggers when:\r\n    - No input/textarea/select elements are focused (to avoid conflicts with typing)\r\n    - The create dialog is not already open\r\n    - No modifiers (Ctrl/Alt/Meta) are pressed\r\n  - Call \u001b[38;2;177;185;249msetCreateDialogOpen(true)\u001b[39m when conditions are met\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m2. Add tests\u001b[22m (frontend/src/components/kanban/KanbanBoard.test.tsx)\r\n  - Test that pressing 'n' opens the create dialog\r\n  - Test that 'n' does NOT trigger when an input is focused\r\n  - Test that 'n' does NOT trigger when the dialog is already open\r\n  - Test that 'N' (uppercase) also works\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mCode Changes\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mLocation:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfrontend/src/components/kanban/KanbanBoard.tsx\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  Add this hook after the other state declarations (around line 80):\r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m// Keyboard shortcut: 'n' to open create dialog\u001b[39m\r\n  useEffect(\u001b[33m() =>\u001b[39m {\r\n    \u001b[34mconst\u001b[39m handleKeyDown = \u001b[33m(event: KeyboardEvent) =>\u001b[39m {\r\n      \u001b[32m// Only trigger "]
[0.000, "o", "if 'n' or 'N' is pressed without modifiers\u001b[39m\r\n      \u001b[34mif\u001b[39m (\r\n        (event.key === \u001b[31m'n'\u001b[39m || event.key === \u001b[31m'N'\u001b[39m) &&\r\n        !event.ctrlKey &&\r\n        !event.metaKey &&\r\n        !event.altKey &&\r\n        !createDialogOpen\r\n      ) {\r\n        \u001b[32m// Don't trigger if user is typing in an input field\u001b[39m\r\n        \u001b[34mconst\u001b[39m activeElement = \u001b[36mdocument\u001b[39m.activeElement\r\n        \u001b[34mconst\u001b[39m isInputFocused =\r\n          activeElement?.tagName === \u001b[31m'INPUT'\u001b[39m ||\r\n          activeElement?.tagName === \u001b[31m'TEXTAREA'\u001b[39m ||\r\n          activeElement?.tagName === \u001b[31m'SELECT'\u001b[39m ||\r\n          activeElement?.getAttribute(\u001b[31m'contenteditable'\u001b[39m) === \u001b[31m'true'\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n        \u001b[34mif\u001b[39m (!isInputFocused) {\r\n          event.preventDefault()\r\n          setCreateDialogOpen(\u001b[34mtrue\u001b[39m)\r\n        }\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    \u001b[36mwindow\u001b[39m.addEventListener(\u001b[31m'keydown'\u001b[39m, handleKeyDown)\r\n    \u001b[34mreturn\u001b[39m \u001b[33m() =>\u001b[39m \u001b[36mwindow\u001b[39m.removeEventListener(\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[31m'keydown'\u001b[39m, handleKeyDown)\r\n  }, [createDialogOpen])\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mTest file:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfrontend/src/components/kanban/KanbanBoard.test.tsx\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  Add test cases to verify the keyboard shortcut functionality.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mBenefits\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  - ✅ Non-intrusive: doesn't affect existing functionality\r\n  - ✅ User-friendly: standard key for \"new\" actions\r\n  - ✅ Safe: won't trigger when typing in fields\r\n  - ✅ Simple: minimal code changes, easy to maintain\r\n  - ✅ Testable: clear behavior to verify\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mAlternative Approaches Considered\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mOption 2: Create a custom \u001b[38;2;177;185;249museKeyboardShortcut\u001b[39m hook\u001b[22m\r\n  - More reusable if multiple shortcuts are needed in the future\r\n  - Slightly more complex for a single shortcut\r\n  - Could be refactored later if more shortcuts are added\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1mOption 3: Use a keyboard shortcut library\u001b[22m (e.g., \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mreact-hotkeys-hook\u001b[39m)\r\n  - Adds external dependency\r\n  - Overkill for a single shortcut\r\n\r\n  Would you lik"]
